    <!-- https://w3id.org/CBGP-App#related-records-definition -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CBGP-App#related-records-definition">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A panel a form shows on an existing record, listing the records of ANOTHER form that point back at it, declared via local:has-related-records. local:related-form is the other form; local:related-via is the field on that other form holding a cross-reference (local:references / local:references-via) to this form - its stored value is matched against this record&apos;s value of the referenced key field. local:related-column (repeatable; shown in the other form&apos;s question-order) selects the columns. Optional aggregate: local:related-sum-field is summed over the rows that are active today (between local:related-active-from-field and local:related-active-to-field, either of which may be blank on a record = unbounded); if local:related-expected-total is given and at least one row is active, a warning is shown when the sum differs from it by more than local:related-tolerance (default 0). By default the key matched is the open record&apos;s value of the field that local:related-via references; local:related-key-field overrides that with a field of the open record itself, for a panel on the related form (e.g. a commitment listing the other commitments of the same member). A definition can be shared by several forms. No form-specific logic lives in code.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">Definición de panel de registros relacionados</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Related records panel definition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


